ord","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLineDetail"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If the staff-lines element is present, the appearance of each line may be individually specified with a line-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"detail type. Staff lines are numbered from bottom to top. The print-object attribute allows lines to be hidden"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within a staff. This is used in special situations such as a widely-spaced percussion staff where a note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"placed below the higher line is distinct from a note placed above the lower line. Hidden staff lines are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included when specifying clef lines and determining display-step \/ display-octave values, but are not counted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as lines for the purposes of the system-layout and staff-layout elements."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLineDetail"}],"title":"MXLLineDetail"}}}